    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290">

                <pb facs="0563" n="429" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg429"/>

                <head>No. 290.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Maury.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-09-14"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 14,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 100.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 136, of the 9th
                    ultimo, in which you refer to the political condition of Colombia, and to the
                    disapproval shown as regards President Nuñez’ offensive reference to foreign
                    Governments, inclosing at the same time the inaugural speech of Dr. Holguin on
                    his assuming the Presidential office.</p>
                <p>Your dispatch has been read with much satisfaction.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
